<title>FINLAND: Borealis says to up Porvoo polyethylene capacity.</title>
<headline>Borealis says to up Porvoo polyethylene capacity.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chemicals group Borealis A/S said on Monday it would increase polyethylene production capacity at its plant in Porvoo, Finland to 140,000 tonnes per year from 120,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>Copenhagen-based Borealis, jointly owned by Finland's Neste Oy and Norwegian Statoil, said the investment would total 35 million markka ($6.9 million) and involve a two-week shut-down in late summer next year.  </p>
<p>Borealis said the increase would improve the quality of its output and the cost-effectiveness of its operations.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +3589 6805 0247, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
